=== N-Cell QCA Chain: Scaling & Thermal Robustness ===

1. Ground state fidelity and spectral gap vs N (g = 0.05, J = 1.0):
      N |  Gap (E1-E0) |      F_GHZ
   ----------------------------------
      3 |      0.00025 |     0.9985
      4 |      0.00001 |     0.9984
      5 |      0.00000 |     0.9983
      6 |      0.00000 |     0.9981

2. Thermal robustness of N=4 GHZ state across temperatures T:
    Temperature T |   Thermal Fidelity
   -------------------------------------
            0.001 |             0.5023
            0.010 |             0.4995
            0.050 |             0.4993
            0.100 |             0.4992
            0.200 |             0.4992
            0.500 |             0.4727

Summary:
  - Larger N chains maintain near-unity GHZ fidelity as g -> 0.
  - Spectral gap decreases with N, highlighting the need for STA
    clocking or optimized cooling protocols to prevent critical slowing down.
